//
// A MATCH THAT LEAVES A VALUE UNCOVERED IS REFUSED (`@FR-M-Total`, with `@FR-M-Unit`).  A guarded
// unit arm does not cover its variant, and slice arms count only with total element patterns and
// no guard, so a length they leave is uncovered.  Each function is one refusal with its
// expectation.
//
// ── a-guarded-unit-arm-does-not-cover-its-variant ──
//
// A GUARDED UNIT ARM DOES NOT COVER ITS VARIANT (`@FR-M-Total` crossed with `@FR-M-Unit`).
// M-Unit: `V` matches an enum value whose variant is the unit variant V.  M-Total: `total(V)`
// is true, but `total(pat if cond) = false` — "a GUARDED arm NEVER secures totality, whatever its
// pattern" — and on an enum subject "a variant counts as covered only by a TOTAL arm"; a variant
// left uncovered with no `_` is a static error naming it.  Here the only arm for `Red` is
// guarded, every other variant has a bare unit arm, and there is no `_`.
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: match on MtC is not exhaustive — missing: Red
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal fires on 18594597b, interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the missing variant.
// HOLDS: `unit-arms-cover-an-enum-without-a-wildcard` beside it.
//
// ── slice-arms-that-leave-a-length-uncovered-are-refused ──
//
// SLICE ARMS THAT LEAVE A LENGTH UNCOVERED ARE REFUSED (`@FR-M-Total`).  The vector clause
// counts an arm only with total element patterns and no guard, and asks that every length be
// covered: a rest arm alone leaves the empty vector out; `[]` with `[x, y, ..rest]` leaves
// length one out; a guard on the rest arm covers nothing (`total(pat if cond) = false`); a
// variant element pattern can fail on the element.  Each is the refusal that holds since
// @PLN35, now worded with the covering spelling.  One function per shape.
//
// @falsified-at: none — the negation cells of a rule that holds; the refusal fires on
//   b36d0449f too, worded without the covering spelling.
// CHANNEL: expect — each function's diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: a build admitting one of these compiles its function and leaves its claim unanswered.
// HOLDS: `head-and-tail-arms-cover-every-length` beside it.

enum MtC { Red, Green, Blue }

fn mt_f(c: MtC, x: integer) -> integer {
  match c {
    Red if x > 0 => 1,
    Green => 2,
    Blue => 3
  }
}

fn test_a_guarded_unit_arm_does_not_cover_its_variant() {
  assert(mt_f(MtC.Green, 1) == 2, "unreachable");
}

enum T { Leaf, Node { v: integer } }

// @EXPECT_ERROR: a slice pattern can fail
fn test_a_rest_arm_alone() {
  v = [1];
  n = match v { [x, ..rest] => x };
  assert(n == 1, "unreachable");
}

// @EXPECT_ERROR: a slice pattern can fail
fn test_a_length_left_out() {
  v = [1];
  n = match v { [] => 0, [x, y, ..rest] => x + y };
  assert(n == 0, "unreachable");
}

// @EXPECT_ERROR: a slice pattern can fail
fn test_a_guarded_rest_arm() {
  v = [1];
  n = match v { [] => 0, [x, ..rest] if x > 0 => x };
  assert(n == 1, "unreachable");
}

// @EXPECT_ERROR: a slice pattern can fail
fn test_a_variant_element() {
  v: vector<T> = [];
  n = match v { [] => 0, [Leaf, ..rest] => 1 };
  assert(n == 0, "unreachable");
}
